# Trivy ignore list.
#
# These HIGH/CRITICAL findings are all in build-time / desktop-only tooling that
# is present in the server images only because the Dockerfiles install the whole
# pnpm workspace:
#
#   * the corepack-managed pnpm 9.12 CLI and its bundled deps (tar, minimatch,
#     brace-expansion, cross-spawn) under /app/.cache/node/corepack/ — used to
#     install dependencies, not exposed by the running api/web/worker processes.
#   * electron — pulled in by apps/desktop; not used by the api/web/worker
#     runtime at all.
#
# Server runtime dependencies are gated separately and strictly by
# `pnpm audit --prod --audit-level=high` in .github/workflows/pr.yml.
#
# Follow-ups that would let us delete this list:
#   * upgrade pnpm to the patched 10.x line and stop shipping the corepack cache;
#   * split prod Dockerfiles so apps/desktop + apps/mobile deps never enter the
#     server images.
#
# NOTE: keep this list to CVE/GHSA ids only. Do not add runtime deps here.

